## Community Co-Investment Funds

These are additional, optional funds designated for community-led co-investment in community-designated development priorities. 

* **Hyku Community Development Co-Investment Fund - **co-invest in feature development for roadmap priorities selected and led by the Hyku Interest Group. 
* **Hyrax/Hyku Maintenance Co-Investment Fund** - Co-invest in critical maintenance by contributing to the Maintenance Co-Investment Fund. Co-investment dollars are used to fund maintenance work including accessibility improvements, component upgrades, and other critical work that is required to keep Samvera software up-to-date.

Email heather@samvera.org to contribute to these funds. 

### Support Samvera via your existing Consortial Membership 

If you use Hyku or other Samvera Community software as a member of a consortium, and you would prefer to support Samvera via contributions to your consortium, you can contribute to your consortium’s Samvera Partnership Fund. 

## New Samvera Partner benefit: the Hyrax and Hyku Upgrade Planning Service

**As institutional budgets face scrutiny, the Samvera Community is looking for ways to directly connect how financial support that sustains the community also returns concrete support to each Partner institution.** Institutions have told us that upgrading to the latest versions of Hyrax and Hyku is an activity where subject expertise could provide efficiency and confidence in the planning stages.

**Samvera Partnership now includes dedicated technical planning support.** Each year, every Partner institution can elect to receive one detailed upgrade plan for a selected Hyrax or Hyku application. This is a focused assessment with a sequenced roadmap for planning, budgeting, and beginning the upgrade process. The plan is created by Rob Kaufman in his community-funded role as Hyrax and Hyku Technical Coordinator.

Ohio State University Libraries participated as a pilot for the upgrade plan process. You can [read their case study](https://samvera.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/samvera/pages/4423745555) to learn about their experience: “We feel more confident moving forward in this endeavor. The upgrade and migration service is a wonderful support to Samvera Partners, and we highly encourage others to take advantage of it. Rob’s analysis is worth every penny of our Partner dues.”

All the details, including an example report table of contents and answers to some frequently asked questions, can be found on the [Hyrax and Hyku Upgrade Planning Service page on the Samvera Community wiki](https://samvera.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/samvera/pages/4423450635/Samvera+Partner+Benefit+Hyrax+and+Hyku+Upgrade+Planning+Service).
